# Picker and worker environment. Copy to ./radio.env and fill in.
# Nothing here is committed; this file holds placeholders only.

# --- paths -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where Liquidsoap pools, queues, history and index.db live.
RADIO_STATE=/state
# Where stations.json and the generated radio.liq live.
RADIO_CONFIG=/config
# Navidrome as a service: the index is paged out of the Subsonic API and tracks
# are played as stream URLs by id. No database access, no music mount.
NAVIDROME_URL=http://172.17.0.1:4533
NAVIDROME_USER=radio
NAVIDROME_PASS=change-me
# Icecast as the picker sees it (inside the compose network this is the mixer).
ICECAST_URL=http://mixer:8000
PORT=8030
# How listeners reach this station, no trailing slash. Used for the icy-url header a
# stream advertises and for nothing else; leave it empty and streams simply go without.
# SPICA_PUBLIC_URL=https://spica.example.com

# --- LLM DJ ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Any OpenAI-compatible chat completions endpoint with tool calling.
LLM_BASE=
LLM_KEY=
LLM_MODEL=
# Optional extra headers, comma separated k=v pairs.
LLM_HEADERS=

# --- optional enrichment -----------------------------------------------------
# Last.fm API key: enables name-based similar artists, and the tag backfill used
# only for artists MusicBrainz has no genres for. Everything works without it, at
# a lower quality. Popularity (ListenBrainz) needs no key at all.
LASTFM_KEY=
# MusicBrainz asks callers to identify themselves. The default is the project's own
# name and URL, which is enough to be polite; put your address here if you would
# rather it pointed at you. Used for similarity lookups and the artist genres that
# decide a track's label.
# MB_USER_AGENT=radio/0.1 ( you@example.com )
